-- COLLISIONS: How Objects Interact in the Game World
-- This file handles detecting when the player overlaps with platforms, fire, coins, and the goal.
-- Collision detection is the backbone of any platformer game.


-- FUNCTION: checkCollisions
-- PARAMETERS: gameState, canvas, callbacks
-- PURPOSE: The master collision function. Called every frame to check all interactions.
-- CONDITIONAL: if the game state is not "playing" then skip all collision checks and return.
-- This prevents collision logic from running on menus or game-over screens.


-- SECTION: Platform Collisions (AABB - Axis-Aligned Bounding Box)

-- HOW COLLISION DETECTION WORKS:
-- Every object in the game is represented as a rectangle with x, y, width, and height.
-- Two rectangles overlap if ALL four of these conditions are true:
--   1. Player's left edge is less than platform's right edge.
--   2. Player's right edge is greater than platform's left edge.
--   3. Player's top edge is less than platform's bottom edge.
--   4. Player's bottom edge is greater than platform's top edge.
-- This is called "AABB collision detection" and is the most common method in 2D games.

-- VARIABLE: allPlatforms
-- TYPE: List of platform objects
-- PURPOSE: Combines static and moving platforms into one list for collision checking.

-- FOR EACH platform in allPlatforms:
--   CONDITIONAL: if player rectangle overlaps platform rectangle then resolve the collision.
--
--   RESOLVING COLLISIONS - Finding the smallest overlap:
--   When the player overlaps a platform, we need to figure out FROM WHICH SIDE.
--   We calculate four overlap distances:
--
--   set overlapTop to (player bottom) minus (platform top).
--   set overlapBottom to (platform bottom) minus (player top).
--   set overlapLeft to (player right) minus (platform left).
--   set overlapRight to (platform right) minus (player left).
--
--   The SMALLEST overlap tells us which side the collision came from.
--   This is called "minimum penetration depth" resolution.
--
--   CONDITIONAL: if smallest overlap is the top AND player is falling down then
--     -- The player landed ON TOP of the platform.
--     set player y to platform top minus player height.
--     set player vertical velocity to 0.
--     set player jumping to false.
--     set player grounded to true.
--     set player lastGroundedTime to the current time.
--     -- MOVING PLATFORM: if this platform has a speed, move the player with it.
--     if platform has speed then add (platform speed times platform direction) to player x.
--
--   CONDITIONAL: if smallest overlap is the bottom AND player is moving up then
--     -- The player hit the UNDERSIDE of the platform (bonked their head).
--     set player y to platform bottom.
--     set player vertical velocity to 0.
--     -- This stops upward momentum, making the player start falling.
--
--   CONDITIONAL: if smallest overlap is the left then
--     -- The player hit the LEFT SIDE of the platform (pushed from the right).
--     set player x to platform left minus player width.
--     set player horizontal velocity to 0.
--     -- WALL DETECTION: if the player is airborne and falling, they are touching a wall.
--     if player is not grounded AND player is falling then set touchingWall to 1.
--     -- touchingWall = 1 means the wall is to the player's RIGHT (they face left to wall-slide).
--
--   CONDITIONAL: if smallest overlap is the right then
--     -- The player hit the RIGHT SIDE of the platform (pushed from the left).
--     set player x to platform right.
--     set player horizontal velocity to 0.
--     if player is not grounded AND player is falling then set touchingWall to negative 1.
--     -- touchingWall = -1 means the wall is to the player's LEFT.


-- SECTION: Fire Collisions

-- VARIABLE: dashInvincible
-- TYPE: Boolean
-- PURPOSE: When the player is dashing, they are immune to fire damage.
-- This is a core game mechanic: the dash is both a movement tool and a survival tool.

-- FOR EACH fire hazard in the fires list:
--   CONDITIONAL: if player is NOT dash-invincible
--     AND player left is less than fire right minus 5
--     AND player right is greater than fire left plus 5
--     AND player top is less than fire bottom
--     AND player bottom is greater than fire top plus 5 then
--       call the onDeath callback.
--
--   NOTE: The "minus 5" and "plus 5" values shrink the fire hitbox slightly.
--   This makes fire collisions more forgiving. The visible flames extend slightly
--   beyond the actual danger zone. This is a common game design trick called
--   "generous hitboxes" that makes the game feel fair.


-- SECTION: Coin Collisions

-- FOR EACH coin in the coins list:
--   CONDITIONAL: if this coin has NOT already been collected
--     AND player overlaps the coin's 20x20 pixel area then
--       set the coin's collected flag to true.
--       call the onCoinCollect callback (adds to score).
--       play the "coin" sound effect.
--       spawn a particle effect at the coin's center position.
--       -- The particle type "coin" creates 8 golden sparkle particles.
--
--   NOTE: Once collected, the coin stays in the list but is skipped in future checks.
--   This is simpler than removing items from a list during iteration.


-- SECTION: Goal Collision

-- The goal is a gate the player must reach to complete the level.
-- CONDITIONAL: if player rectangle overlaps goal rectangle then
--   call the onWin callback.
-- This is a simple overlap check with no special resolution needed.
-- Touching the goal in any way triggers level completion.


-- SECTION: Boundary Collisions

-- These keep the player inside the visible game area.
-- CONDITIONAL: if player x is less than 0 then set player x to 0.
--   This prevents the player from walking off the left edge of the screen.
-- CONDITIONAL: if player right edge exceeds canvas width then clamp to canvas width.
--   This prevents walking off the right edge.
-- CONDITIONAL: if player y is greater than canvas height then call onDeath.
--   If the player falls below the bottom of the screen, they die.
--   There is no floor at the bottom. Falling off the world is lethal.
